#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Still service for the radxa-cam node: raw NV12 frames from the ISP main path.

    GET /still?frames=N   N raw NV12 frames 3280x2464 from /dev/video0, back to back
    GET /still?frames=N&fresh=1[&skip=K][&settle=M][&keep=S]
                          series mode: the main path keeps streaming between
                          requests, the answer is the next N frames whose
                          exposure started after the request came in
    GET /series/stop      stop the series stream now (otherwise it stops by itself)
    GET /focus            focus set-up page (cam-still 3): live full-resolution crops + sharpness
    GET /focus/stream?rects=x,y,w,h;...&ov=8
                          endless stream of FCS1 packets, the newest frame each time
    GET /status           JSON: busy, device, size, autoexposure, series, focus

Runs permanently (systemd unit cam-still.service) and replaces the per-shot ssh
upload of still_grab.py. It is deliberately dumb: it never chooses exposure or
gain - those are set through the panel (cam-panel, :8080, POST /api/camera) -
and it does no processing. Averaging, colour, black level and PNG are done on
the PC (host/still.py, or a client application).

The capture is exactly still_grab.py's (docs/radxa-zero3.md, "Measurement
still"):
  * v4l2-ctl --stream-mmap=4 --stream-skip=PRE+POST --stream-count=N --stream-to=-
    writes the frames straight into the client socket; Python never touches
    the pixel data (a Python relay tops out at ~90 MB/s, v4l2-ctl hits the
    gigabit ceiling at ~116 MB/s);
  * after PRE frames the CURRENT sensor controls are written back as "the
    neighbour value, then the value itself" - right after a pipeline start the
    sensor may not hold the cached value, and v4l2 does not write a value that
    equals its cache. The values are the ones read before the capture, so the
    service still does not choose anything;
  * POST more frames are discarded while the controls settle (measured: 4 is
    enough even with a full v4l2 queue).

It must never disturb the live stream: the stream runs on the self path
(/dev/video1) and both ISP outputs work in parallel. If the stream sits on the
main path itself (modes wider than 1920), the service refuses with 503 instead
of stopping it - still.py stops the stream in that case, this service does not.
The codec and RGA are never involved (docs/radxa-zero3.md, pitfall 1); the
sensor mode is never pinned (pitfall 2); frame sizes must be multiples of 16.

Response body (Content-Length is exact, so a short read on the client side
means the capture broke):
    "STL1"                  4 bytes, magic
    uint32 LE               length L of the JSON header
    L bytes UTF-8 JSON      {"format":"NV12","width","height","stride",
                             "frame_bytes","frames","skip","controls":{...},
                             "device","service"}
    frames x frame_bytes    NV12: Y plane (height rows x stride), then the
                            interleaved UV plane (height/2 rows x stride)

Series mode (cam-still 2, 2026-09-30). A measurement series (for example, a
calibration grid of a moving light spot) takes dozens of short stills in a row; restarting v4l2-ctl for each one
costs ~0.9 s (set-fmt, get-ctrl, first frame 0.17 s, warm-up 0.5 s). With
fresh=1 the service starts ONE v4l2-ctl stream on the main path and keeps it
until no fresh request came for `keep` seconds (default 10, max 60):
  * v4l2-ctl writes frames into a pipe, a reader thread keeps the last RING
    frames with their sequence numbers; the time a frame was dequeued comes
    from the '<' marks on stderr;
  * a request waits for frames dequeued after it arrived, drops `skip` of them
    (default 2: the first one may have started exposing before the request -
    the scene was still changing) and `settle` more if the client has just
    changed the controls through the panel (like POST), then sends N frames;
  * at stream start the controls are reasserted after the first frame and 4
    frames are dropped, exactly like the one-shot capture;
  * a request without fresh=1 stops the series first and then works as before,
    so old clients see no difference; an old service ignores fresh=1, so a new
    client works with it too (just slower);
  * the pipe relay is Python (~90 MB/s, docs/radxa-zero3.md): for the 1-2
    frames of a series shot that is 0.13-0.27 s, much less than the restart.

Focus mode (cam-still 3, 2026-10-20). The compressed live stream is useless for
judging focus, the full frame is 12 MB. /focus/stream rides the series stream
and sends, for the newest frame each time (frames in between are dropped, so a
slow client never builds a backlog), the Y bytes of up to 8 crops (side 16..512,
pushed inside the frame) and a Y overview decimated by ov (2/4/8/16, 0 - none):
    "FCS1", uint32 LE length L, L bytes JSON {"seq","dropped","fps","controls",
    "width","height","rects":[[x,y,w,h]...],"overview":[w,h,step]?,"service"},
    then the crops row by row in order, then the overview.
It holds LOCK while it runs (stills get 409 busy naming the focus client); a new
/focus/stream takes over from the previous one, which ends on its next frame.
A client gone silently is dropped by a 5 s send timeout. The page (GET /focus)
computes sharpness in the browser.

Errors are JSON {"error": code, "message": text}:
    400 bad_request      bad parameters
    409 busy             another capture is running (one at a time)
    409 autoexposure     rkaiq_3A is running - switch to manual via the panel
    503 main_path_busy   the live stream itself is on /dev/video0
    500 capture_failed   v4l2-ctl failed before streaming started

Standard library only: the board may sit on a network with no internet.
"""
import argparse
import fcntl
import http.server
import json
import re
import socket
import socketserver
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
import urllib.parse

VERSION = "cam-still 3"
MAGIC = b"STL1"

ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()
ap.add_argument("--port", type=int, default=8081)
ap.add_argument("--bind", default="0.0.0.0")
ap.add_argument("--device", default="/dev/video0", help="ISP main path")
ap.add_argument("--width", type=int, default=3280)
ap.add_argument("--height", type=int, default=2464)
ap.add_argument("--max-frames", type=int, default=128)
ap.add_argument("--v4l2-ctl", default="v4l2-ctl",
                help="path to v4l2-ctl; tests/fake_v4l2ctl.py for tests without a camera")
ap.add_argument("--no-system-checks", action="store_true",
                help="skip the rkaiq_3A / main-path checks (tests without systemd)")
ap.add_argument("--ring", type=int, default=8, help="series mode: frames kept in memory (fresh requests take up to ring-2)")
A = ap.parse_args()

if A.width % 16 or A.height % 16:
    sys.exit("frame size must be a multiple of 16 (docs/radxa-zero3.md, RGA pitfall)")

# Same neighbourhood as still_grab.py: exposure-1, again-1, dgain+1 for the
# default measurement mode; stepping down unless already at the minimum.
CTRL_MIN = {"exposure": 0, "analogue_gain": 256, "gain": 256}
CTRLS = ("exposure", "analogue_gain", "gain")

LOCK = threading.Lock()


def log(*m):
    print(*m, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


def run(args, timeout=10):
    return subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)


def autoexposure_on():
    if A.no_system_checks:
        return False
    return run(["systemctl", "is-active", "rkaiq_3A"]).stdout.strip() == "active"


def main_path_user():
    """The live stream's gst pipeline, if it reads the main path itself."""
    if A.no_system_checks:
        return ""
    r = run(["pgrep", "-af", "v4l2src device=%s " % A.device])
    return r.stdout.strip()


def get_controls():
    r = run([A.v4l2_ctl, "-d", A.device, "--get-ctrl=" + ",".join(CTRLS)])
    vals = {}
    for line in r.stdout.splitlines():
        m = re.match(r"\s*(\w+)\s*:\s*(-?\d+)", line)
        if m and m.group(1) in CTRLS:
            vals[m.group(1)] = int(m.group(2))
    return vals if len(vals) == len(CTRLS) else None


def set_controls(vals):
    arg = ",".join("%s=%d" % (k, vals[k]) for k in CTRLS)
    subprocess.run([A.v4l2_ctl, "-d", A.device, "--set-ctrl=" + arg],
                   check=True, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=sys.stderr, timeout=10)


def set_format(w, h):
    """Set NV12 WxH on the main path and read back stride / image size."""
    r = run([A.v4l2_ctl, "-d", A.device, "--set-fmt-video=width=%d,height=%d,pixelformat=NV12" % (w, h)])
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError("set-fmt: " + (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-300:])
    r = run([A.v4l2_ctl, "-d", A.device, "--get-fmt-video"])
    text = r.stdout
    gw = re.search(r"Width/Height\s*:\s*(\d+)/(\d+)", text)
    if not gw or (int(gw.group(1)), int(gw.group(2))) != (w, h):
        raise RuntimeError("the driver did not accept %dx%d NV12: %s" % (w, h, text.strip()[-300:]))
    if "NV12" not in text:
        raise RuntimeError("pixel format is not NV12: " + text.strip()[-300:])
    bpl = re.search(r"Bytes per Line\s*:\s*(\d+)", text)
    stride = int(bpl.group(1)) if bpl else w
    # Frame size in the stream: v4l2-ctl --stream-to writes bytesused of every
    # buffer, and still.py has always read exactly w*h*3/2 per frame (3280x2464
    # packed) without losing sync. Size Image is only reported for diagnostics.
    frame_bytes = stride * h * 3 // 2
    si = re.search(r"Size Image\s*:\s*(\d+)", text)
    if si and int(si.group(1)) != frame_bytes:
        log("warning: Size Image %s != stride*h*3/2 = %d" % (si.group(1), frame_bytes))
    return stride, frame_bytes


def read_exact(f, view):
    """Fill the memoryview from the pipe; False on EOF."""
    got = 0
    while got < len(view):
        k = f.readinto(view[got:])
        if not k:
            return False
        got += k
    return True


class Series:
    """One long v4l2-ctl stream on the main path for fresh=1 requests (module docstring)."""

    POST = 4          # frames dropped after the start-up reassert, as in the one-shot capture

    def __init__(self):
        self.cond = threading.Condition()
        self.proc = None
        self.error = None
        self.seq = 0              # frames fully read from the pipe
        self.marks = []           # dequeue times from '<' on stderr, index = frame number - 1
        self.valid_from = 1       # first frame number with the controls settled
        self.keep_until = 0.0
        self.clients = 0
        self.slots = []
        self.pinned = None
        self.stride = self.frame_bytes = 0
        self.ctl = None
        self.started = 0.0

    def running(self):
        return self.proc is not None and self.proc.poll() is None and self.error is None

    def status(self):
        with self.cond:
            return {"running": self.running(), "frames": self.seq, "error": self.error,
                    "keep_s": round(max(0.0, self.keep_until - time.monotonic()), 1),
                    "age_s": round(time.monotonic() - self.started, 1) if self.running() else None}

    def start(self, keep):
        """Start the stream if it is not running; returns an error text or None. Caller holds LOCK."""
        with self.cond:
            self.keep_until = max(self.keep_until, time.monotonic() + keep)
            if self.running():
                return None
        self.stop()
        w, h = A.width, A.height
        stride, frame_bytes = set_format(w, h)
        ctl = get_controls()
        cmd = [A.v4l2_ctl, "-d", A.device,
               "--set-fmt-video=width=%d,height=%d,pixelformat=NV12" % (w, h),
               "--stream-mmap=4", "--stream-to=-"]
        proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, bufsize=0)
        try:
            fcntl.fcntl(proc.stdout.fileno(), 1031, 1 << 20)     # F_SETPIPE_SZ: fewer wake-ups per 12 MB frame
        except OSError:
            pass
        with self.cond:
            self.proc, self.error, self.seq, self.marks = proc, None, 0, []
            self.valid_from = 1 + 1 + self.POST
            self.stride, self.frame_bytes, self.ctl = stride, frame_bytes, ctl
            # [buffer, frame number (-1 while being written)]
            self.slots = [[bytearray(frame_bytes), 0] for _ in range(max(4, A.ring))]
            self.scratch = bytearray(frame_bytes)
            self.pinned = None        # (first, last) frame numbers a request is sending
            self.started = time.monotonic()
            self.keep_until = time.monotonic() + keep
        threading.Thread(target=self._read_frames, args=(proc,), daemon=True).start()
        threading.Thread(target=self._read_marks, args=(proc, ctl), daemon=True).start()
        threading.Thread(target=self._watch, args=(proc,), daemon=True).start()
        log("SERIES start %dx%d, controls %s, keep %.0f s" % (w, h, ctl, keep))
        return None

    def stop(self, why="stop"):
        with self.cond:
            proc, self.proc = self.proc, None
            self.cond.notify_all()
        if proc is not None:
            if proc.poll() is None:
                proc.kill()
            proc.wait()
            log("SERIES %s after %d frames" % (why, self.seq))

    def _fail(self, proc, text):
        with self.cond:
            if self.proc is proc and self.error is None:
                self.error = text
            self.cond.notify_all()

    def _read_marks(self, proc, ctl):
        err = bytearray()
        n = 0
        while True:
            c = proc.stderr.read(1)
            if not c:
                break
            if c != b"<":
                err += c
                continue
            n += 1
            with self.cond:
                if self.proc is not proc:
                    return
                self.marks.append(time.monotonic())
                self.cond.notify_all()
            if n == 1 and ctl:
                # right after a pipeline start the sensor may not hold the cached value (module docstring)
                try:
                    set_controls({k: v - 1 if v > CTRL_MIN[k] else v + 1 for k, v in ctl.items()})
                    set_controls(ctl)
                except Exception as e:
                    log("series reassert failed: %s" % e)
        if proc.poll() is None or proc.wait() != 0:
            self._fail(proc, "v4l2-ctl stopped: " + err.decode(errors="replace").strip()[-300:])

    def _read_frames(self, proc):
        f = proc.stdout
        while True:
            with self.cond:
                if self.proc is not proc:
                    return
                slot = self.slots[self.seq % len(self.slots)]
                # a slow client is still sending the frame in this slot: drop the new frame instead
                keep = self.pinned is not None and self.pinned[0] <= slot[1] <= self.pinned[1]
                if not keep:
                    slot[1] = -1      # being overwritten
            if not read_exact(f, memoryview(self.scratch if keep else slot[0])):
                self._fail(proc, "stream ended")
                return
            with self.cond:
                self.seq += 1
                if not keep:
                    slot[1] = self.seq
                self.cond.notify_all()

    def pin(self, first, n, on):
        """Keep frames first..first+n-1 from being overwritten while they are sent (n <= ring - 2)."""
        with self.cond:
            self.pinned = (first, first + n - 1) if on else None

    def _watch(self, proc):
        last, t_last = -1, time.monotonic()
        while True:
            time.sleep(0.5)
            with self.cond:
                if self.proc is not proc:
                    return
                now = time.monotonic()
                if self.seq != last:
                    last, t_last = self.seq, now
                idle = self.clients == 0 and now > self.keep_until
                stalled = now - t_last > 5
            if stalled:
                self._fail(proc, "no frames for 5 s")
                self.stop("stalled")
                return
            if idle:
                self.stop("idle")
                return

    def frame(self, number, deadline):
        """Wait for frame `number` (1-based); returns the slot buffer or raises."""
        with self.cond:
            while self.seq < number:
                if self.error or self.proc is None:
                    raise RuntimeError(self.error or "series stopped")
                left = deadline - time.monotonic()
                if left <= 0:
                    raise RuntimeError("frame %d did not come in time (have %d)" % (number, self.seq))
                self.cond.wait(left)
            slot = self.slots[(number - 1) % len(self.slots)]
            if slot[1] != number:
                raise RuntimeError("frame %d was overwritten: the client reads slower than the camera" % number)
            return slot

    def latest(self, after, deadline):
        """Newest settled frame with a number > after: (number, slot). Frames in between are dropped (focus mode)."""
        with self.cond:
            while self.seq <= after or self.seq < self.valid_from:
                if self.error or self.proc is None:
                    raise RuntimeError(self.error or "series stopped")
                left = deadline - time.monotonic()
                if left <= 0:
                    raise RuntimeError("no new frame in time (have %d)" % self.seq)
                self.cond.wait(left)
            return self.seq, self.slots[(self.seq - 1) % len(self.slots)]

    def fps(self):
        with self.cond:
            m = self.marks[-11:]
        return round((len(m) - 1) / (m[-1] - m[0]), 2) if len(m) >= 3 and m[-1] > m[0] else None

    def first_fresh(self, t_req, skip, settle, deadline):
        """Number of the first frame to send: dequeued after t_req, minus skip/settle."""
        with self.cond:
            while True:
                if self.error or self.proc is None:
                    raise RuntimeError(self.error or "series stopped")
                after = [i + 1 for i, t in enumerate(self.marks) if t > t_req]
                if after:
                    return max(after[0] + skip + settle, self.valid_from)
                left = deadline - time.monotonic()
                if left <= 0:
                    raise RuntimeError("no frame after the request")
                self.cond.wait(left)


SERIES = Series()

# Focus mode (cam-still 3): one client at a time; a new /focus/stream takes over from the old one
FOCUS = {"gen": 0, "client": None, "since": None, "packets": 0}
FOCUS_LOCK = threading.Lock()
FOCUS_MAX_RECTS = 8
FOCUS_RECT = (16, 512)          # side of a crop, px
FOCUS_STEPS = (0, 2, 4, 8, 16)  # overview decimation; 0 - no overview


def parse_rects(text, w, h):
    """'x,y,w,h;x,y,w,h' -> [(x, y, w, h)], clipped into the frame; ValueError on nonsense."""
    rects = []
    for part in filter(None, text.split(";")):
        x, y, rw, rh = (int(v) for v in part.split(","))
        if not (FOCUS_RECT[0] <= rw <= FOCUS_RECT[1] and FOCUS_RECT[0] <= rh <= FOCUS_RECT[1]):
            raise ValueError("crop side %d..%d" % FOCUS_RECT)
        rw, rh = min(rw, w), min(rh, h)
        rects.append((min(max(x, 0), w - rw), min(max(y, 0), h - rh), rw, rh))
    if len(rects) > FOCUS_MAX_RECTS:
        raise ValueError("at most %d crops" % FOCUS_MAX_RECTS)
    return rects


def focus_packet(buf, stride, w, h, rects, step, head):
    """One frame of the focus stream: Y of each crop and a decimated Y overview, no copies of the whole frame."""
    parts = []
    for x, y, rw, rh in rects:
        parts.append(b"".join(buf[(y + r) * stride + x:(y + r) * stride + x + rw] for r in range(rh)))
    if step:
        ow, oh = len(range(0, w, step)), len(range(0, h, step))
        parts.append(b"".join(buf[r * stride:r * stride + w:step] for r in range(0, h, step)))
        head["overview"] = [ow, oh, step]
    head["rects"] = [list(r) for r in rects]
    js = json.dumps(head).encode()
    return [FOCUS_MAGIC, struct.pack("<I", len(js)), js] + parts


FOCUS_MAGIC = b"FCS1"


class Handler(http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
    protocol_version = "HTTP/1.1"
    server_version = VERSION

    def log_message(self, fmt, *args):
        log("%s %s" % (self.address_string(), fmt % args))

    def _json(self, code, obj):
        data = json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False).encode("utf-8")
        self.send_response(code)
        self.send_header("Content-Type", "application/json; charset=utf-8")
        self.send_header("Content-Length", str(len(data)))
        self.send_header("Cache-Control", "no-store")
        self.end_headers()
        self.wfile.write(data)

    def _error(self, code, err, msg):
        self._json(code, {"error": err, "message": msg})

    def _busy(self):
        who = FOCUS["client"]
        self._error(409, "busy", "focus mode is running (%s), close /focus" % who if who
                    else "another capture is running")

    def _page(self, html):
        data = html.encode("utf-8")
        self.send_response(200)
        self.send_header("Content-Type", "text/html; charset=utf-8")
        self.send_header("Content-Length", str(len(data)))
        self.send_header("Cache-Control", "no-store")
        self.end_headers()
        self.wfile.write(data)

    def do_GET(self):
        u = urllib.parse.urlparse(self.path)
        q = urllib.parse.parse_qs(u.query)
        if u.path == "/status":
            self._json(200, {"service": VERSION, "busy": LOCK.locked(), "device": A.device,
                             "width": A.width, "height": A.height, "max_frames": A.max_frames,
                             "autoexposure": autoexposure_on(), "series": SERIES.status(),
                             "focus": {"active": FOCUS["client"] is not None, "client": FOCUS["client"],
                                       "since": FOCUS["since"], "packets": FOCUS["packets"]}})
        elif u.path == "/still":
            self.still(q)
        elif u.path == "/focus":
            self._page(FOCUS_PAGE)
        elif u.path == "/focus/stream":
            self.focus_stream(q)
        elif u.path == "/series/stop":
            with LOCK:
                SERIES.stop()
            self._json(200, {"ok": True, "series": SERIES.status()})
        else:
            self._error(404, "not_found", u.path)

    def still(self, q):
        t_req = time.monotonic()
        try:
            n = int(q.get("frames", ["16"])[0])
            pre = int(q.get("pre", ["1"])[0])
            post = int(q.get("post", ["4"])[0])
            reassert = q.get("reassert", ["1"])[0] != "0"
            fresh = q.get("fresh", ["0"])[0] == "1"
            skip = int(q.get("skip", ["2"])[0])
            settle = int(q.get("settle", ["0"])[0])
            keep = float(q.get("keep", ["10"])[0])
        except ValueError:
            return self._error(400, "bad_request", "frames/pre/post/skip/settle must be integers, keep a number")
        if not (1 <= n <= A.max_frames) or not (1 <= pre <= 10) or not (0 <= post <= 30):
            return self._error(400, "bad_request",
                               "frames 1..%d, pre 1..10, post 0..30" % A.max_frames)
        if not (0 <= skip <= 10) or not (0 <= settle <= 30) or not (1 <= keep <= 60):
            return self._error(400, "bad_request", "skip 0..10, settle 0..30, keep 1..60")
        if fresh and n > max(4, A.ring) - 2:
            return self._error(400, "bad_request", "fresh: frames 1..%d (ring %d)" % (max(4, A.ring) - 2, max(4, A.ring)))
        if not LOCK.acquire(blocking=False):
            return self._busy()
        try:
            if fresh:
                self.capture_fresh(n, skip, settle, keep, t_req)
            else:
                SERIES.stop("one-shot request")
                self.capture(n, pre, post, reassert)
        finally:
            LOCK.release()

    def series_refusal(self):
        """The checks of the one-shot path, once per series: True if an error was sent."""
        if SERIES.running():
            return False
        if autoexposure_on():
            self._error(409, "autoexposure", "rkaiq_3A is running; switch to manual exposure via the panel (:8080)")
            return True
        who = main_path_user()
        if who:
            self._error(503, "main_path_busy", "the live stream reads %s itself (mode wider than 1920?): %s"
                        % (A.device, who[:160]))
            return True
        return False

    def focus_stream(self, q):
        """Endless stream of FCS1 packets: Y crops at full resolution + a decimated overview, newest frame each time.

        Takes over from a previous focus client (the browser reconnects when the crops change). Holds LOCK while
        it runs: stills get 409 busy, focus mode is a set-up mode of its own."""
        w, h = A.width, A.height
        try:
            rects = parse_rects(q.get("rects", [""])[0], w, h)
            step = int(q.get("ov", ["8"])[0])
            if step not in FOCUS_STEPS:
                raise ValueError("ov one of %s" % (FOCUS_STEPS,))
            if not rects and not step:
                raise ValueError("nothing to send: no crops and no overview")
        except ValueError as e:
